The PANACEA project aims to tackle complex, interrelated climate risks and adaptation challenges by integrating diverse methodologies. Current approaches—ranging from process-based models to econometric techniques—often operate in silos, creating gaps in understanding systemic risks. Utilizing innovative machine learning and computational Bayesian modeling, PANACEA will bridge these fields to provide a comprehensive understanding of critical climate risks, including flooding impacts, biodiversity loss, crop damages, and macroeconomic implications. The project emphasizes adaptation, investigating how local interactions and unexpected climate events affect various sectors. By focusing on four targeted areas, PANACEA seeks to enhance adaptation strategies while refining future climate risk assessments. Ultimately, this interdisciplinary initiative aims to create a robust framework that supports resilient responses to an increasingly unpredictable climate landscape.
